@page "/packs"
@inherits ActionPage
@inject PortalApi Api
<PageTitle>Maintained scenario packs — Retry Assurance</PageTitle><span class="eyebrow">VERSIONED INPUT · EXPLICIT ADOPTION</span><h1>The actual scenario pack</h1><p class="lede">A bounded executable server behavior, not an AI-generated description or an arbitrary customer script.</p><StatusMessage Text="@Message" Error="@Failed" />
@foreach(var pack in Items){<section class="pack"><div class="title-row"><h2>@pack.Title</h2><span class="tag">@pack.Id@@@pack.Version</span></div><p>@pack.Description</p><ol class="steps"><li>The real client sends one synthetic JSON create request with its client-owned operation key.</li><li>The service commits the request journal and resource effect atomically.</li><li>For the first accepted request, acknowledgement headers are withheld for @pack.DelayMs milliseconds.</li><li>An internal retry using the same key and payload reuses the resource. A fresh key creates another resource.</li><li>Finalization closes admission before evaluating the durable resource count and declared terminal policy.</li></ol><dl class="facts"><div><dt>Allowed route</dt><dd>@pack.Operation.Method @pack.Operation.Path</dd></div><div><dt>HTTP attempt budget</dt><dd>@pack.MaxAttempts</dd></div><div><dt>Scenario</dt><dd>@pack.Scenario</dd></div><div><dt>Evidence version</dt><dd>@pack.EvidenceVersion</dd></div></dl><details><summary>Immutable content identity</summary><code class="digest">@pack.Hash</code><p>Each execution records this exact pack hash. A different pack or behavior contract is not presented as a controlled before/after comparison.</p></details></section>}
<section class="scope-callout"><h2>Bounded coverage</h2><p>The first pack tests duplicate effects under delayed acknowledgement for one declared operation. It does not claim TLS failure simulation, all-provider API compatibility or universal retry correctness. A safe terminal uncertainty remains distinct from server-proven effects.</p></section>
@code{List<ScenarioPack> Items=[];protected override Task OnInitializedAsync()=>Act(async()=>{Items=(await Api.GetAsync<PackList>("packs")).Packs;});}
